  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "To satisfy the use case of controlling a puppet menu while simultaneously locomoting with joysticks, optionally controlling puppet xy (what the joystick would have inputted) instead via relative wrist rotation might work. Basically how smart TVs with accelerometers in the remote control can use that rotation to drive an \"air cursor\".\nI'm thinking it should probably clamp if the wrist is rotated too far, and then as soon as you rotate back the previous max clamp is now the max value and it immediately moves back away from the edge of the puppet dial in that new reference frame.",
